{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22069 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "Cocosamide B is implicated in the biological pathway leading to CCF-STTG1 through a series of target relationships. The evidence suggests that Cocosamide B directly targets VMRC-LCP, which in turn is a target of Glycitein and another compound, (1R,2R,4S,7Z,11R)-4,8-dimethyl-12-methylidene-3,14-dioxatricyclo[9.3.0.02,4]tetradec-7-en-13-one. All these compounds ultimately have CCF-STTG1 as their target. This indicates a potential cascade of interactions where Cocosamide B may influence the activity of VMRC-LCP, which then modulates the function of CCF-STTG1. The shared target relationship among these compounds suggests a possible mechanism involving the regulation of a common downstream effector, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a pathway where Cocosamide B could act as a modulator of VMRC-LCP, which in turn affects CCF-STTG1, highlighting a potential role in cellular signaling or metabolic regulation.",
